ran King would come on after Blubaugh, surrendering another two runs in the second inning to put the Astros behind 3-0.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>Miguel Ullola would quiet things for a bit, before Colson Montgomery hit a home run to straight away center to extend the lead to 4-0 White Sox. An infield single in the fifth would add another, making it a five-run deficit.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>Nelson Velazquez though would not go quietly, as he crushed a pinch-hit two run homer to bring it back to a 5-2 White Sox lead. Chicago would add another un on a wild pitch to make it 6-2. The Astros would add one back with a Jose Altuve infield single. Yainer Diaz would come up as the tying run in the 8th but struck out looking.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>The White Sox were led by great pitching from Hagen Smith, who went 3.0 IP, allowing just two hits. Grant Taylor closed the game out, pitching the final two innings, allowing one unearned run on two hits.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>The Astros trail the series 1-0 and must win Wednesday to force a decisive Game Three. First pitch is at 4 pm at Daikin Park.\u003c/p>\n\n","schedule":{},"type":"html"},{"attributes":{"mimetype":"image/jpeg","type":"image"},"bucket":"assets.getty","caption":"HOUSTON, TEXAS - SEPTEMBER 29: Jeremy Peña #3 of the Houston Astros walks back to the dugout after flying out in the third inning against the Chicago White Sox in game one of the American League Wild Card Series at Daikin Park on September 29, 2026 in Houston, Texas. (Photo by Kenneth Richmond/Getty Images)","id":"%2F6abc6f547fe4fb32aee4223a","new_tab":false,"schedule":{},"source_credit":"Kenneth Richmond / Getty Images Sport / Getty Images","title":"American League Wild Card Series: Chicago White Sox v Houston Astros - Game One","type":"asset","url":"","use_caption":false}],"canonical_url":"https://ktrh.iheart.com/featured/houston-texas-news/content/2026-09-29-astros-on-brink-of-elimination-after-6-3-loss-to-white-sox-in-game-one-of-wild-card-series/","cuser":"user/ld