{"ref_id":"%2F6abbe897d124ab43a84698ef","type":"content","payload":{"amp_enabled":true,"apple_news":null,"author":"","blocks":[{"html":"\u003cp>\u003cstrong>The lawyer for Lindsay Clancy told the judge at a hearing Tuesday morning that the prosecution didn't present evidence that Clancy was in a relatively normal state of mind or indeed was not suffering from psychosis at the time her children were killed.\u003c/strong>\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>Clancy and her attorney were in the Plymouth, Massachusetts courtroom to decide the future direction of legal actions, after last week's mistrial in the case, in which the 36-year-old is charged with 3 counts of murder in the January 2023 deaths of her children.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>The defense attorney, Kevin Reddington, told the judge there was not sufficient evidence provided in court that Clancy killer the three children, and therefore the case must be dismissed \u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>Reddington is also angling for Judge William Sullivan to overrule the recent mistrial verdict and declare Clancy not guilty, based on the precedent of the landmark US Supreme Court case Jackson v. Virginia, which would require the judge to rule not guilty in favor of Clancy since there was not enough evidence to prove her state of mind was anything but psychotic.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>In addition to a not guilty ruling, Reddington asked the judge for a further dismissal of the case.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>Prosecutors stated that they met the burden of proof in the case, and later Tuesday called Reddington's argument that there was not enough evidence against Clancy &quot;laughable.&quot;\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>The prosecution has not said publicly whether it intends to retry the case.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>All parties will be back in court November 2nd to discuss the motions by Clancy's lawyer.\u003c/p>\n\n","schedule":{},"type":"html"},{"id":"2361","kind":"station","related_id":"","schedule":{},"type":"catalog"}],"canonical_url":"https://ktrh.iheart.com/feat