upport the use of force to prevent Trump from being president","targets":[],"title":"Nearly Half Of Democrats Are Okay With Violence To Stop President Trump","permalink":"https://ktrh.iheart.com/featured/houston-texas-news/content/2026-09-28-nearly-half-of-democrats-are-okay-with-violence-to-stop-president-trump/"},"slug":"2026-09-28-nearly-half-of-democrats-are-okay-with-violence-to-stop-president-trump","summary":{"image":"https://i.iheart.com/v3/re/assets.getty/6aba9ea17d252db2ba0cf74f","title":"Nearly Half Of Democrats Are Okay With Violence To Stop President Trump","description":"The survey found that 25% of American adults support the use of force to prevent Trump from being president","author":"B.D. Hobbs"},"pub_start":1790673769415,"pub_until":4115978604802,"pub_changed":1790673772952,"subscription":[{"tags":["categories/local-news","brands/Houston & Texas News","brands/San Antonio's First News","brands/KTRH-AM (700)","brands/WOAI-AM (1229)","brands/KFXR-AM (7513)"]}],"exclusion":[{"tags":[]}],"linksData":[],"lookup":["publish_origin:brands/Houston & Texas News","id:/6aba9dbaec8fcaa9a9382735","slug:2026-09-28-nearly-half-of-democrats-are-okay-with-violence-to-stop-president-trump","slug:2026-09-28-nearly-half-of-democrats-are-okay-with-violence-to-stop-president-trump","author:user"]}},{"id":"%2F6abaebb1b5c6d14c66f5eb23","type":"PUBLISHING","record":{"ref_id":"%2F6abaebb1b5c6d14c66f5eb23","type":"content","payload":{"amp_enabled":true,"apple_news":null,"author":"Corey Olson","blocks":[{"html":"\u003cp>Not that Democrats were begging her to do so, but former Vice President Kamala Harris has \u003ca href=\"https://nypost.com/2026/09/26/us-news/kamala-harris-hits-midterm-campaign-trail-but-some-dems-are-begging-ex-vp-to-just-stay-home/?shem=aimgspe\" target=\"_blank\">returned to the campaign trail\u003c/a> ahead of the midterms. Harris appeared last week alongside Michigan U.S. Senate candidate Abdul El-Sayed at a bizarre roundtable event about black health care. During the event, Harris delivered one of her signature word salads, talking about the importance of &quot;what black people and black birthing people need in order to move themselves forward.&quot;\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>At another recent campaign event, Harris shared this deep thought: &quot;When we feel powerless, we are powerless...when we feel powerful, we are powerful.&quot;\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>Harris is also scheduled to appear at campaign events in Georgia and Nevada, so we can expect more quotables. But many Democrats are telling her to stay away. &quot;She's been turned down a lot,&quot; a Dem campaign source told the New York Post. A Democcrat Senate candidate in Kansas flatly rejected Harris' help when asked if he would welcome her. &quot;I would say please do not come to my state, I do not need you here,&quot; he told NBC News.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>&quot;There are definitely mixed feelings about her,&quot; says \u003ca href=\"https://faculty.tarleton.edu/kabala/\" target=\"_blank\">Dr. Bo Kabala\u003c/a>, political science professor at Tarleton State University. &quot;She can pack a room, and she's got the celebrity connections on the left. But when it comes to connecting with everyday voters and connecting on a policy level, I think doubts remain.&quot;\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>Still, Harris has an odd appeal among mainstream Democrats. Polls have consistently had her \u003ca href=\"https://ktrh.iheart.com/featured/houston-texas-news/content/2026-02-16-cant-quit-kamala-harris-leads-dem-28-polls/\" target=\"_blank\">at or near the top\u003c/a> of Democrat presidential candidates for 2028, and California Gov. Gavin Newsom recently said he would not run in '28 if Harris does.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>Add it all up, and the best way to describe Kamala Harris's relationship with the Democratic Party is &quot;it's complicated.&quot; &quot;It's complicated because she is a vice president---that title stays with you---and she stepped into a difficult situation for the party in 2024,&quot; says Kabala. &quot;But in terms of the connection and in terms of really presenting a vision for the Democratic Party, I think privately---and increasingly publicly---by a 60-40 or 70-30 margin, the Democratic Party does not want her to be the nominee.&quot;\u003c/p>\n\n","schedule":{},"type":"html"},{"attributes":{"mimetype":"image/jpeg","type":"image"},"bucket":"new_assets","caption":"LOS ANGELES, CALIFORNIA - SEPTEMBER 29: Former U.S. Vice President Kamala Harris walks onstage before speaking at the Wiltern Theatre on September 29, 2025 in Los Angeles, California. Harris is in the midst of a 15-city book tour following the release of ","id":"%2F691e133f33fa7ab25c80fdb2","new_tab":false,"schedule":{},"source_credit":"Getty Images North America","title":"","type":"asset","url":"","use_caption":false},{"attributes":{"@provider":"iHeartRadio","@query":"https://www.iheart.com/oembed/?format=json&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.iheart.com%2Flive%2Ffox-news-radio-8627%2F","@url":"https://www.iheart.com/live/fox-news-radio-8627/","author_name":"Fox News Radio","author_url":"https://www.iheart.com/live/fox-news-radio-8627/","fixedWidth":450,"height":200,"html":"\u003ciframe title=\"Fox News Radio\" height=\"200\" width=\"100%\" src=\"https://www.iheart.com/live/fox-news-radio-8627/?embed=true&cid=oembed&keyid%5B0%5D=Fox%20News%20Radio&sc=live_widget\" allow=\"autoplay\" frameborder=\"0\">\u003c/iframe>","provider_name":"iHeartRadio","provider_url":"https://www.iheart.com","thumbnail_height":300,"thumbnail_url":"https://i.iheart.com/v3/re/new_assets/5f3b43f0529439aac0159456?ops=fit(300%2C300)","thumbnail_width":300,"title":"Fox News Radio","type":"rich","version":"1.0","width":"100%"},"embed_type":"rich","html":"\u003ciframe title=\"Fox News Radio\" height=\"200\" width=\"100%\" src=\"https://www.iheart.com/live/fox-news-radio-8627/?embed=true&cid=oembed&keyid%5B0%5D=Fox%20News%20Radio&sc=live_widget\" allow=\"autoplay\" frameborder=\"0\">\u003c/iframe>","provider":"iHeartRadio","rendering_hint":"default","schedule":{},"type":"embed","url":"https://www.iheart.com/live/fox-news-radio-8627/"}],"canonical_url":"https://ktrh.iheart.com/featured/houston-texas-news/content/2026-09-28-help-not-wanted-dem-candidates-reject-kamalas-return/","cuser":"user/ldap/ccrhou1cpo","enable_featured_widget":true,"exclusion":{"tags":[]},"external_url":"","fb_allow_comments":true,"featured_widget":{"country":"","id":"","kind":"","related_id":""},"feed_content_id":"","feed_partner_content":false,"feed_permalink":"","feed_type":"","feed_vendor":"","include_recommendations":true,"include_video_monetization":true,"is_sponsored":false,"keywords":["keywords/Kamala Harris","keywords/Democrats","keywords/campaign trail","keywords/midterms","keywords/politics","keywords/election"],"primary_image":{"bucket":"new_assets","id":"%2F691e133f33fa7ab25c80fdb2"},"primary_target":{"categories":["categories/local-news"],"distribution":["brands/Houston & Texas News","brands/San Antonio's First News","brands/KTRH-AM (700)","brands/WOAI-AM (1229)","brands/KFXR-AM (7513)"]},"publish_date":1790673752931,"publish_end_date":4115978604802,"publish_origin":"brands/Houston & Texas News","seo_title":"","show_updated_timestamp":false,"simplereach_enabled":false,"slug":"2026-09-28-help-not-wanted-dem-candidates-reject-kamalas-return","social_title":"","summary":"Former Vice President Kamala Harris is back on the campaign trail, whether Democrats want her there or not.","targets":[],"title":"Help Not Wanted: Dem Candidates Reject Kamala's Return","permalink":"https://ktrh.iheart.com/featured/houston-texas-news/content/2026-09-28-help-not-wanted-dem-candidates-reject-kamalas-return/"},"slug":"2026-09-28-help-not-wanted-dem-candidates-reject-kamalas-return","summary":{"image":"https://i.iheart.com/v3/re/new_assets/691e133f33fa7ab25c80fdb2","title":"Help Not Wanted: Dem Candidates Reject Kamala's Return","description":"Former Vice President Kamala Harris is back on the campaign trail, whether Democrats want her there or not.","author":"Corey Olson"},"pub_start":1790673752931,"pub_until":4115978604802,"pub_changed":1790673758951,"subscription":[{"tags":["categories/local-news","brands/Houston & Texas News","brands/San Antonio's First News","brands/KTRH-AM (700)","brands/WOAI-AM (1229)","brands/KFXR-AM (7513)"]}],"exclusion":[{"tags":[]}],"linksData":[],"lookup":["publish_origin:brands/Houston & Texas News","id:/6abaebb1b5c6d14c66f5eb23","slug:2026-09-28-help-not-wanted-dem-candidates-reject-kamalas-return","slug:2026-09-28-help-not-wanted-dem-candidates-reject-kamalas-return","keyword:keywords/Kamala Harris","keyword:keywords/Democrats","keyword:keywords/campaign trail","keyword:keywords/midterms","keyword:keywords/politics","keyword:keywords/election","author:user"]}},{"id":"%2F6abb12ec04804560772ddff9","type":"PUBLISHING","record":{"ref_id":"%2F6abb12ec04804560772ddff9","type":"content","payload":{"amp_enabled":true,"apple_news":null,"author":"Andre Perrard","blocks":[{"html":"\u003cp>For the longest time now, many congressional districts around the country have been baked into one political party. Some are considered always to be safe either red or blue. But midterms can always shake things up, and Republicans are having to treat these midterms no differently. Even as the Democrats continue proving why they are an insane option every day.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>Because of the current political climate, media, and narcissistic politicians, the GOP is in a pickle. The Republicans have not advanced President Trump's agenda to people's liking, mostly due to spineless self-interest. But the war with Iran has not helped President Trump, at least in the eyes of some, as people are upset over gas prices and housing.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>So, now the GOP is having to pour millions of dollars from their war chest into \u003ca href=\"https://www.newsmax.com/newsfront/election-money-republicans/2026/09/27/id/1270827/\" target=\"_blank\">some races that are generally seen as safe red.\u003c/a> One of those is right here in Texas, as Monica De La Cruz seeks re-election in the 15th District. She is facing off with Democrat Bobby Pulido, a Tejano musician and celebrity in south Texas. That seat is currently seen as a &quot;tossup&quot; according to the Cook Political Report.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>Political strategist Bill Miller says this race being tight is not a surprise, as Pulido's name recognition helps him.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>&quot;Him being on the ballot makes that race competitive, and De La Cruz is going to have to work hard if she wants to return to Congress,&quot; he says.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>The GOP has pumped $2 million into De La Cruz's race. That district was won by President Trump in 2024 by 18 points. While that is concerning, it is also part of the midterm games. The majority party, in this case Republicans, historically always lose seats in the midterms. The battle was already going to be tough, but facing someone with Pulido's influence makes it tougher.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>But that is also just part of where Republicans are at the moment, facing a crossroads of history and potential voter discouragement.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>&quot;The environment for Republicans has become one of a question rather than a sure thing...but we are in the home stretch,&quot; says Miller. &quot;The question is what do voters do going into early voting...do they come home? Are they angry about things? That is the environmental question.&quot;\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>Americans too, at least a vast majority, are very gullible. They will buy anything the media tells them to. In reality, things are trending absolutely in the right direction. They could be better, but we are seeing positive trends economically and otherwise.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>However, If CNN says they should be mad at Trump about gas prices, they follow suit. It is a society of sheep rather than wolves. Which makes the GOP's job even tougher. Because breaking through years of propaganda is not something done overnight. If Republicans cannot get their messaging through to the public, then all the money in the world will not stop what is coming.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>&quot;Are they unhappy about the state of the nation? If so, Republicans are at real risk...if they acknowledge things are okay, but they could be better, races in Texas will remain Republican,&quot; Miller says.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp>Miller says De La Cruz does have an advantage over Pulido, that being the fact she has experience in politics.\u003c/p>\n\n","schedule":{},"type":"html"},{"attributes":{"mimetype":"image/jpeg","type":"image"},"bucket":"assets.getty","caption":"DALLAS, TEXAS - SEPTEMBER 09: U.S. Rep. Monica De La Cruz (R-TX) speaks on the first day of the 2026 Republican National Convention at the American Airlines Center on September 09, 2026 in Dallas, Texas. U.S. President Donald Trump will headline the Republican National Committee's first-ever midterm convention as he aims to highlight his administration’s achievements and rally support for GOP candidates just two months before the upcoming elections being held on November 3. (Photo by Alex Wong/Getty Images)","id":"%2F6abb138e7d540a262d624b59","new_tab":false,"schedule":{},"source_credit":"Kevin Dietsch / Getty Images News / Getty Images","title":"Republicans Gather In Dallas For Inaugural Midterm Convention","type":"asset","url":"","use_caption":false}],"canonical_url":"https://ktrh.iheart.com/featured/houston-texas-news/content/2026-09-28-republicans-pour-money-into-texas-race-generally-considered-safe-red/","cuser":"user/ldap/1135944","enable_featured_widget":true,"exclusion":{"tags":[]},"external_url":"","fb_allow_comments":true,"featured_widget":{"country":"","id":"","kind":"","related_id":""},"feed_content_id":"","feed_partner_content":false,"feed_permalink":"","feed_type":"","feed_vendor":"","include_recommendations":true,"include_video_monetization":true,"is_sponsored":false,"keywords":["keywo